quran[13]{c,v,t}:
  43,48,"We did not show them any sign, but it was greater (in significance) than the previous one, which was similar to it. And We seized them with punishment; perhaps they might return (to the right path)."
  43,49,And they would say: ‘O magician! Invoke your Lord for us by virtue of the covenant He made with you. (Then) surely we will be guided.’
  43,50,"But as soon as We removed the punishment from them (responding to Moses’ prayer), behold, they would break their pledge."
  43,51,"Pharaoh called out among his people, saying: ‘O my people! Does not the kingdom of Egypt belong to me? And these rivers that flow beneath my feet (are not mine also)? Can you not see?"
  43,52,Am I not better than this humble one who can hardly express himself?
  43,53,"Why have golden bracelets (of kingship) not been cast upon him, and why have the angels not come with him as (his) attendants?’"
  43,54,"So he fooled his people, and they obeyed him. Indeed, they were a transgressing people."
  43,55,"So when they roused Our wrath, We took vengeance upon them and drowned them all together."
  43,56,"Thus, We made them a thing of the past and an example for those after them."
  43,57,"And when the son of Maryam (Mary) is cited as an example (in argument), behold, your people laugh at it (mockingly)."
  43,58,"They say: ‘Are our gods better or he?’ They do not cite him to you but to dispute. No doubt, they are a contentious people."
  43,59,He (Jesus) was just a servant whom We had blessed with (Our) favour. And We made him an exemplar for the Children of Israel.
  43,60,"Had We willed, We would have made angels from you to be (your) successors upon the earth."
